WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.844
A content type needs places to keep its data, such as a name,

00:00:04.844 --> 00:00:06.852
a number of seats, or a date.

00:00:06.852 --> 00:00:09.032
Content fields are those places.

00:00:09.032 --> 00:00:12.761
In this video you add six kinds of field to a content type,

00:00:12.761 --> 00:00:14.080
and fill them in.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.221
A content type describes one kind of content on your site, such as a workshop.

00:00:23.221 --> 00:00:26.573
It is built from parts, and the fields you add to a type

00:00:26.573 --> 00:00:29.600
are kept in a part with the same name as the type.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.824
A field holds a named piece of data.

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:37.596
Its field type decides what it stores, its settings decide what it accepts,

00:00:37.596 --> 00:00:40.600
and its editor decides how people fill it in.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.254
The Content Fields feature provides the common field types.

00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:47.056
A Text Field holds text.

00:00:47.056 --> 00:00:51.020
A Numeric Field holds a number, and can limit it to a range.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.115
A Boolean Field holds yes or no.

00:00:54.115 --> 00:00:57.878
A Date Field, a Date Time Field and a Time Field hold a

00:00:57.878 --> 00:01:00.840
day, a day with a time, and a time of day.

00:01:05.054 --> 00:01:08.376
Let's check that the Content Fields feature is on.

00:01:08.376 --> 00:01:11.640
Under Tools, Features, search for Content Fields.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.268
The Enabled badge confirms it, and an Enable button turns the feature on

00:01:16.268 --> 00:01:17.514
when it is off.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:20.518
Let's add the fields to a content type.

00:01:20.518 --> 00:01:25.630
Under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, this site has a type named Workshop,

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.596
and its Edit button opens it.

00:01:27.596 --> 00:01:30.180
A separate video covers creating a type.

00:01:30.643 --> 00:01:34.681
The Fields section is empty, and Add Field starts the first one.

00:01:34.681 --> 00:01:37.335
The Parts list shows only Title for now.

00:01:37.335 --> 00:01:43.103
The first field creates a part named Workshop, which contains the fields for the current type.

00:01:47.358 --> 00:01:51.332
On the Workshop type, Add Field opens a form with a Display Name,

00:01:51.332 --> 00:01:53.570
a Technical Name and a Field Type.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:57.209
The Technical Name follows the Display Name as you type it.

00:01:57.209 --> 00:01:59.168
Let's call the field Speaker.

00:01:59.627 --> 00:02:03.924
The Field Type list shows the fields that the enabled features provide.

00:02:03.924 --> 00:02:08.278
Let's choose Text Field, and then Save & Configure, which adds the field

00:02:08.278 --> 00:02:09.897
and opens its settings.

00:02:10.395 --> 00:02:16.143
A Text Field has settings such as Required, Hint, Placeholder, Default value, Minimum

00:02:16.143 --> 00:02:18.164
length and Maximum length.

00:02:18.164 --> 00:02:23.975
Two lists below choose the editor and the display mode, which a separate video covers.

00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:29.311
Let's make the field required, and add a hint that says who leads the workshop.

00:02:29.311 --> 00:02:34.299
Save returns to the type, where Speaker is listed with the field type Text Field.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.653
A Numeric Field holds a number.

00:02:40.653 --> 00:02:45.230
On the Workshop type, let's add a field named Seats, choose Numeric Field

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:48.880
as its type, and open the settings with Save & Configure.

00:02:49.332 --> 00:02:55.041
Scale is the number of digits after the decimal point, and zero accepts whole numbers only.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:59.691
Minimum and Maximum limit the range, and Default value fills the box when

00:02:59.691 --> 00:03:01.162
you create an item.

00:03:01.631 --> 00:03:05.824
A workshop room has limited seats, so let's require a value from one

00:03:05.824 --> 00:03:07.864
to forty, and start at twenty.

00:03:07.864 --> 00:03:09.621
Save returns to the type.

00:03:13.886 --> 00:03:18.656
A Boolean Field holds a yes or no value, which appears as a checkbox.

00:03:18.656 --> 00:03:24.826
On the Workshop type, let's add Registration Open as a Boolean Field and open its settings.

00:03:25.293 --> 00:03:27.896
Label is the text beside the checkbox.

00:03:27.896 --> 00:03:32.984
Default value is true decides whether it starts checked when you create an item.

00:03:32.984 --> 00:03:38.663
Let's set the label to Participants can register, turn on Default value is true, and save.

00:03:42.869 --> 00:03:45.474
A Date Field holds a day without a time.

00:03:45.474 --> 00:03:49.778
On the Workshop type, let's add Registration Deadline as a Date Field.

00:03:49.778 --> 00:03:54.139
Beyond the two lists, its settings are Required and Hint, so let's save

00:03:54.139 --> 00:03:55.159
it as it is.

00:03:55.617 --> 00:03:58.161
A Date Time Field holds a day and a time.

00:03:58.161 --> 00:04:02.383
It stores them in Coordinated Universal Time, and shows them in the time

00:04:02.383 --> 00:04:03.628
zone of the site.

00:04:03.628 --> 00:04:06.227
Let's add Starts At, and save it as it is.

00:04:06.685 --> 00:04:09.719
A Time Field holds a time of day, with no date.

00:04:09.719 --> 00:04:11.265
Let's add Doors Open.

00:04:11.265 --> 00:04:17.105
Its settings include a Step, which sets whether the time input accepts seconds and milliseconds.

00:04:17.564 --> 00:04:20.983
The type lists its six fields in the order they were added, each

00:04:20.983 --> 00:04:23.034
with its field type beside the name.

00:04:27.263 --> 00:04:32.195
Under Content, Content Items, the New menu lists the content types you can create.

00:04:32.195 --> 00:04:33.763
Let's choose Workshop.

00:04:34.237 --> 00:04:38.223
The editor for a workshop lists the fields in the order they were

00:04:38.223 --> 00:04:41.142
added, each with the input that fits its type.

00:04:41.142 --> 00:04:45.240
A red asterisk marks Speaker and Seats as required, and the hint of

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.317
Speaker appears with its field.

00:04:47.807 --> 00:04:53.546
Seats starts at twenty, its default value, with the minimum and the maximum beside the input.

00:04:53.546 --> 00:04:59.517
The checkbox labeled Participants can register starts checked, because its default value is true.

00:05:00.002 --> 00:05:02.366
Let's enter a title and the speaker.

00:05:02.366 --> 00:05:06.475
Then, to see validation at work, let's enter a seat count of fifty,

00:05:06.475 --> 00:05:08.332
which is above the maximum.

00:05:08.796 --> 00:05:13.948
The date, the date and time, and the time use the inputs that your browser provides.

00:05:13.948 --> 00:05:18.298
Let's enter a registration deadline, a start date and time, and a time

00:05:18.298 --> 00:05:19.786
when the doors open.

00:05:20.276 --> 00:05:23.557
Publish checks every field against its settings.

00:05:23.557 --> 00:05:29.086
The Numeric Field refuses fifty, so the editor stays open and shows an error message.

00:05:29.625 --> 00:05:33.293
Let's change the seat count to twenty-five and publish again.

00:05:33.293 --> 00:05:36.085
The item is saved, and a message confirms it.

00:05:40.249 --> 00:05:43.443
The Content Items list shows the workshop you published.

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:47.101
View opens it on the site, where the fields print their values in

00:05:47.101 --> 00:05:49.059
the order they have in the type.

00:05:49.529 --> 00:05:54.050
By default, these fields print their value alone, without the field name.

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:58.342
The Text Field prints its text, the Numeric Field its number, and the

00:05:58.342 --> 00:06:00.689
Boolean Field prints True or False.

00:06:01.147 --> 00:06:03.398
The Date Field prints only the day.

00:06:03.398 --> 00:06:06.966
The Date Time Field prints the day and the time in the time

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.228
zone of the site.

00:06:08.228 --> 00:06:11.247
The Time Field prints hours, minutes and seconds.

00:06:13.247 --> 00:06:18.367
Content fields keep typed values in a content type, such as text, numbers,

00:06:18.367 --> 00:06:24.063
yes or no, dates and times, with settings for required values, limits and defaults.

00:06:24.063 --> 00:06:25.727
Thanks for watching.

